{
 "result": "fibmod.py is a table-based fast-doubling solver. It reduces n modulo P = 2(M+1) (Pisano bound), splits n into h = n>>16 and l = n&65535, and combines precomputed fib values F(l) and F(h*65536) from tables. Per-token memoization and byte-level stdin reading. It passes the public sample (in-0 output is byte-identical to out-0) and is registered at baseline 13.22 (noise 2.5%). Resting here: the body is already near the cost floor for this approach, prior variants in the lineage gave no gain beyond noise, and a further win needs more than 3% which would not justify the thinking cost.",
